# P3.3 handover — snapshot jobs, import controls and audit search

P3.G2 was accepted on 2026-08-18 through change-log entry C-P3.2-D after the
complete independent implementation and security review recorded in
`docs/review/phase-3-p3-2-submission.md` §11. P3.3 may now begin; no later Phase 3
gate is accepted by that decision.

Before implementing P3.3, read `.agents/AGENTS.md`, the complete Phase 3 section
of `docs/implementation-plan.md`, and the accepted P3.0 contracts. Baseline P3.3
as its own package with named ownership, estimates, environment readiness,
review/remediation allowance and its stop-gate evidence.

P3.3 owns the durable background-job and snapshot-import control surfaces that
P3.2 deliberately leaves absent: bounded upload/admission, immutable artifact
identity, preview/apply job lifecycle, current-role rechecks at apply, stale
preview invalidation, idempotency and concurrency, Council/Admin separation,
audit search, raw-artifact authorization, runtime-role denials, restart/recovery,
and the measured asynchronous preview constraint. Do not turn on game-state
corrections or write an unmigrated legacy field.

Preserve the P3.2 boundaries now accepted:

- R-20–R-38 and their authorization matrix remain authoritative;
- C-04 remains temporary, Google-read-only and outside the portal runtime;
- only the latest C-04 run may be decided;
- R-37 serializes account-wide identity changes and cannot strand an account;
- no Phase 3 route mutates character game state; and
- P3.3 must pass independent implementation and distinct security-focused
  review before its own gate may close.
